Dear all,

I'm a newly R-user, so forgive me if this is a naive question.

At the bottom of this message I put some data about seed growth in 6 maize genotypes (sorry for such a long message). I'm interested in fitting linear-with-plateau functions (piecewise, non-linear model) to describe seed growth. I know how to do it with each separate group (genotype) the following way:

seedgrth.R18 <- subset(seedgrth, genotype%in%"R18")
linear.plateau <- function(TT, a, b, c) {
ifelse(TT > c, a + b * c, a + b * TT)
}
model.linear.plateau <- nls(SW ~ linear.plateau(TT, a, b, c), data = seedgrth.R18,
start = list(a = 0, b = 0.3, c = 900),
trace = T, control = list(warnOnly = T,
minFactor = 1/2048))

But (here come my questions), is there any possible way of fitting a model like this to each of the facets? I understand that I can add any possible "formula" inside geom_smooth, but is there any "method" for non-linear models?

Thanks in advance!

Alan Severini.

