For the ggplot2 version, I went to the ggplot2 folder in the dir specified by '.Library'  and copied this out of the 'DESCRIPTION' file:

Package: ggplot2
Type: Package
Title: An implementation of the Grammar of Graphics
Version: 0.5.7
Date: 2007-08-28
Author: Hadley Wickham <h.wi...@gmail.com>
Maintainer: Hadley Wickham <h.wi...@gmail.com>
Description: An implementation of the grammar of graphics in R. It
        combines the advantages of both base and lattice graphics:
        conditioning and shared axes are handled automatically, and you
        can still build up a plot step by step from multiple data
