I was trying to get rid of the zero since there weren't any in the data.
Fernando Gonzalez found that this works:

ggplot(statpkgs, aes(Software, PageRank) ) +
   geom_point(size=4) +
   geom_segment( aes(Software, PageRank, xend=Software, yend=0) ) +
   scale_x_discrete("Analytical Software") +
   scale_y_continuous("Google PageRank of Web Site") +

   scale_y_continuous(  ) +
   coord_flip(ylim = c(1,10))

Thanks,
Bob

