oh yeah, I realized I should have done this just before reading your
email.

Everything in the example is the same except below the last comment.
You can get the error by using this instead, because none of the
contours are on the plot:

breaks=c(-10,900,1100)

x11()
print(g + stat_contour(data=FL[[1]],
aes(x=x,y=y,z=z,colour=..level..),

                       breaks=breaks, size=2 ) +
scale_colour_gradient(breaks=breaks) )

Also, setting the breaks in the scale does solve the legend problem
(even if it feels redundant!)

breaks=c(-10,15,30,60,900)

x11()
print(g + stat_contour(data=FL[[1]],
aes(x=x,y=y,z=z,colour=..level..),

                       breaks=breaks, size=2 ) +
scale_colour_gradient(breaks=breaks) )

